# Core Operating Principles

- Understand before editing. Prefer minimal diffs.
- Stability over speed. No unnecessary rewrites or refactors.
- If task is broad or risky, produce a short plan first.
- Documentation is part of the deliverable when behavior changes.
- Use checkpoints for intermediate experimentation. Git history must remain meaningful.
- **Anti-hallucination**: Never invent project facts, architecture details, domain rules, deployment assumptions, or business workflows. Only derive them from real repository evidence, existing docs, or explicit user instructions.
- **Foundation governance**: If a project needs to diverge from a core foundation rule, document the exception explicitly in project rules instead of silently modifying the foundation principle.
- **Autonomous execution**: Run commands and complete workflows yourself. See `.cursor/rules/core/04-autonomous-execution.mdc`. Do not hand routine CLI work to the user.
